We'll build an **end-to-end IMDb movie classification system**:

1. Train multiple ML models on the IMDb rating dataset (predicting the movie **genre** category).  
2. Build a **website** where users enter movie details (rating, votes, runtime, year) and the system uses *all trained ML models* to classify the new input into a genre category, and **segregates results by that category**.

---

## 1. Dataset & Assumption

We use a typical IMDb movie dataset (e.g., `IMDb movies.csv` from Kaggle) with columns:

| Column   | Type    | Example    |
|----------|---------|------------|
| `Title`  | string   | Inception  |
| `Genre`  | string   | Sci-Fi (target)  |
| `Rating` | float    | 8.8        |
| `Votes`  | int      | 2000000    |
| `Runtime` | int years? minutes   | 148          |
| `Year`    | int      | 2010        |

> If your dataset has a different target (e.g., "Rating Category = High / Medium / Low"), just change `target_column` accordingly. The pipeline remains identical.

